Package: adaptsurv
Title: Simulate Bayesian Adaptive Two-Arm Survival Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Adrian", "Wurm", , "352921927+adrianwurm@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates randomised two-arm trials with a time-to-event
    endpoint and compares two designs: a fixed design analysed once with the
    log-rank test, and a Bayesian adaptive design based on conjugate Gamma
    priors for exponential hazard rates, with interim analyses allowing
    early stopping for efficacy or futility. Decision thresholds are
    calibrated by simulation to a one-sided type I error of 2.5%. Scenarios
    with non-proportional hazards are supported.
